Stop [E3005]: #Post contract failed: result must exceed the original amount
  --> PostBreach.jet:4 in discount
    |
4 | #Post(result > cents, "result must exceed the original amount")
    | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `#Pre` (argument claim, checked at entry) or `#Post` (`result` claim, checked before return) condition evaluated false at runtime. `#Post contract failed: result must exceed the original amount` is the clause's own message string. Checked in every build (not a debug/release split) — with file:line.
 Fix: Fix the caller (a failed `#Pre` means an argument violated the function's stated contract) or the function body (a failed `#Post` means it broke its own promise about the result).
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3005
